<title>USA: Railroads top list of firms hurt by UPS strike - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Railroads top list of firms hurt by UPS strike - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. railroads top the list of companies that stand to lose should the three-day strike at United Parcel Service continue, the Wall Street Journal reported in its &quot;Heard on the Street&quot; column.</p>
<p>The paper said in its electronic edition that railroad companies depend on UPS as one of their largest customers.</p>
<p>CSX and Burlington Northern are among railroads that stand to be hurt by the strike, according to the paper.</p>
<p>Other losers if the strike continues include Gateway 2000, Spiegel, Lands' End and J.C. Penney, the paper said.</p>
<p>Winners if the strike continues include Federal Express, Caliber System, Airborne Freight, Yellow Corp, Roadway Express, CF Motor Freight and CNF Transportation, according to the paper.</p>
